1
00:04:17,777 --> 00:04:23,777
Prepare for glory!

2
00:08:35,555 --> 00:08:41,555
300 is a action, adventure, war film directed by Zack Snyder.

3
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:59,333
Based on Frank Miller's graphic novel, "300" is very loosely based the 480 B.C.

4
00:17:11,111 --> 00:17:17,111
Battle of Thermopylae, where the King of Sparta led his army against the advancing Persians; the battle is said to have
inspired all of Greece to band together against the Persians, and helped usher in the world's first democracy.

5
00:21:28,888 --> 00:21:34,888
King Leonidas, played by Gerard Butler.

6
00:25:46,666 --> 00:25:52,666
Gorgo, played by Lena Headey.

7
00:30:04,444 --> 00:30:10,444
Theron, played by Dominic West.

8
00:34:22,222 --> 00:34:28,222
Dilios, played by David Wenham.

9
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Captain, played by Vincent Regan.

10
00:42:57,777 --> 00:43:03,777
Stelios, played by Michael Fassbender.

11
00:47:15,555 --> 00:47:21,555
300 is a 2006 American epic historical action film directed by Zack Snyder,
who co-wrote the screenplay with Kurt Johnstad and Michael B.

12
00:51:33,333 --> 00:51:39,333
It is based on the 1998 Dark Horse comic book limited series of
the same name by Frank Miller and Lynn Varley.

13
00:55:51,111 --> 00:55:57,111
The film, like its source material, is a fictionalized retelling of
the Battle of Thermopylae in the Greco-Persian Wars.

14
01:00:08,888 --> 01:00:14,888
The plot revolves around King Leonidas (Gerard Butler), who leads 300 Spartans into battle against the
Persian "God-King" Xerxes (Rodrigo Santoro) and his invading army of more than 300,000 soldiers.

15
01:04:26,666 --> 01:04:32,666
As the battle rages, Queen Gorgo (Lena Headey) attempts to
rally support in Sparta for her husband.

16
01:08:44,444 --> 01:08:50,444
The film also features Michael Fassbender in his film debut.

17
01:13:02,222 --> 01:13:08,222
The story is framed by a voice-over narrative by the
Spartan soldier Dilios (David Wenham).

18
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
As an unreliable narrator, Dillos introduces various historical inaccuracies and other
fantastical elements, placing 300 within the genre of historical fantasy.

19
01:21:37,777 --> 01:21:43,777
300 was filmed mostly with a superimposition chroma key technique
to replicate the imagery of the original comics.

20
01:25:55,555 --> 01:26:01,555
An unfinished cut of 300 premiered at the Austin
Butt-Numb-A-Thon on December 9, 2006.

21
01:30:13,333 --> 01:30:19,333
The completed film then premiered at the Berlin International Film Festival on February 14, 2007, before being released
in both conventional and IMAX screens in the United States on March 9, and on home media on July 31.

22
01:34:31,111 --> 01:34:37,111
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised its visuals and style but received criticism from historians, who
criticized its historical inaccuracies, most notably its depiction of the Persians, which some characterized as Persophobic.

23
01:38:48,888 --> 01:38:54,888
Grossing over $468.8 million, the film's opening was the 24th-largest in box office
history at the time, and became the tenth highest-grossing film of 2007.

24
01:43:06,666 --> 01:43:12,666
The film earned a leading ten nominations at the 34th Saturn Awards, winning two for
Best Action, Adventure, or Thriller Film and Best Director (for Snyder).

25
01:47:24,444 --> 01:47:30,444
A sequel, titled Rise of an Empire, based on Miller's previously unpublished
graphic novel prequel Xerxes, was released on March 7, 2014.

26
01:51:42,222 --> 01:51:48,222
The film explores themes of army, narration, grave, gore, based on true story.
